<title>NORWAY: Dyno top executive quits.</title>
<headline>Dyno top executive quits.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arild Ingierd, President and Chief Executive Officer of Norwegian explosives and chemicals group Dyno Industrier ASA, announced his resignation on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In a statement to the Oslo Bourse, the company said Ingierd would step down on April 1.</p>
<p>It said he would be succeeded by Dag Mejdell, 39, now Executive Vice President, Finances.</p>
<p>Ingierd has been with Dyno 25 years, including nearly seven years as CEO, and thought it was time to resign, the statement said. He will however continue as a consultant for the company.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
